      "message": "My interpretation of \"the sideband channel of a router to operate as a USB4\nsideband channel, the link over an active cable should be unidirectional\" was that we should not be entering into USB4 mode if the cable isn\u0027t uni-directional.\n\nBut on discussion with the internal teams - It looks like with bi-directional LSRX cables can train the link in uni-direction as well. So even if the tbt cable supports bi-directional link training, we need to set the retimer and mux to uni-direction for operation in USB4 mode.\n\nSorry about the confusion!",
